1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,160
Got a lot of GMail labels?

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:04,319
Here's what your sidebar looks like.

3
00:00:05,050 --> 00:00:08,621
A long, long list, and you've already read almost all of it!

4
00:00:10,133 --> 00:00:13,748
Meet the open envelope, right in the toolbar above your messages.

5
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:16,458
Hover for Toggle Read/Unread.

6
00:00:16,458 --> 00:00:17,358
Now click it!

7
00:00:18,867 --> 00:00:21,103
Before the click, every single label.

8
00:00:21,817 --> 00:00:25,246
After the click, only labels with unread mail, counts and all!

9
00:00:25,950 --> 00:00:29,268
Their folders stay too, so you always know where a label lives.

10
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:32,820
Click again, and everything's back.

11
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:34,435
Nothing is moved or deleted.

12
00:00:35,150 --> 00:00:38,009
And it remembers your choice the next time GMail loads!

13
00:00:38,717 --> 00:00:43,189
From the extension's menu, choose to hide read labels, read mail, or both.

14
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:45,201
Want it?

15
00:00:45,201 --> 00:00:51,591
Find Toggle Read and Unread Labels and Mail in GMail in the Chrome Web Store, and click Add to Chrome.

16
00:00:52,317 --> 00:00:54,658
Reload GMail, and the button is ready.

17
00:00:54,658 --> 00:00:55,766
Nothing to set up!

18
00:00:57,267 --> 00:01:02,177
It only runs on GMail, asks for no extra permissions, and never touches your mail.

19
00:01:02,883 --> 00:01:05,993
It's free and open source, at github.

20
00:01:05,993 --> 00:01:08,011
com/dblock/gmail-toggle.

21
00:01:08,011 --> 00:01:09,944
Enjoy a tidier sidebar!
